    gameId: 'hearts',
    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. PASSING: After the deal, each player selects 3 cards to pass to an opponent (direction rotates: Left, Right, Across, None). All passes are simultaneous.\n2. OPENING LEAD: The player with the 2 of Clubs leads it to the first trick.\n3. FOLLOWING SUIT: Players must follow the suit led if possible. If unable to follow suit, any card may be played (except penalty cards on the first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. There is no trump suit. The trick winner leads the next trick.\n5. BREAKING HEARTS: Hearts cannot be led until a heart has been played ('discarded') on a previous trick, or the player has nothing but hearts remaining.\n6. FIRST TRICK RESTRICTION: No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) may be played on the first trick.\n7. SCORING: After all 13 tricks are played, each player counts penalty points in their captured tricks. Each heart = 1 point, Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points.\n8. SHOOT THE MOON: If one player captures ALL 13 hearts AND the Queen of Spades, they score 0 and every other player scores 26 points.\n9. GAME END: Play continues across rounds until a player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest score at that point wins.",
    Player: "1. PASSING: After the deal, each player selects 3 cards to pass to an opponent (direction rotates: Left, Right, Across, None). All passes are simultaneous.\n2. OPENING LEAD: The player with the 2 of Clubs leads it to the first trick.\n3. FOLLOWING SUIT: Players must follow the suit led if possible. If unable to follow suit, any card may be played (except penalty cards on the first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. There is no trump suit. The trick winner leads the next trick.\n5. BREAKING HEARTS: Hearts cannot be led until a heart has been played ('discarded') on a previous trick, or the player has nothing but hearts remaining.\n6. FIRST TRICK RESTRICTION: No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) may be played on the first trick.\n7. SCORING: After all 13 tricks are played, each player counts penalty points in their captured tricks. Each heart = 1 point, Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points.\n8. SHOOT THE MOON: If one player captures ALL 13 hearts AND the Queen of Spades, they score 0 and every other player scores 26 points.\n9. GAME END: Play continues across rounds until a player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest score at that point wins.",
    objective: 'Have the lowest cumulative score when any player reaches 100 points. Avoid taking tricks containing hearts (1 point each) and the Queen of Spades (13 points).',
    gameplay: "1. PASSING: After the deal, each player selects 3 cards to pass to an opponent (direction rotates: Left, Right, Across, None). All passes are simultaneous.\n2. OPENING LEAD: The player with the 2 of Clubs leads it to the first trick.\n3. FOLLOWING SUIT: Players must follow the suit led if possible. If unable to follow suit, any card may be played (except penalty cards on the first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. There is no trump suit. The trick winner leads the next trick.\n5. BREAKING HEARTS: Hearts cannot be led until a heart has been played ('discarded') on a previous trick, or the player has nothing but hearts remaining.\n6. FIRST TRICK RESTRICTION: No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) may be played on the first trick.\n7. SCORING: After all 13 tricks are played, each player counts penalty points in their captured tricks. Each heart = 1 point, Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points.\n8. SHOOT THE MOON: If one player captures ALL 13 hearts AND the Queen of Spades, they score 0 and every other player scores 26 points.\n9. GAME END: Play continues across rounds until a player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest score at that point wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible; if void in the led suit, may play any card (with first-trick restrictions).',
      "Hearts cannot be led until 'broken' (a heart has been played on a previous trick).",
      'No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) on the first trick.',
      'Queen of Spades = 13 penalty points; each heart = 1 penalty point.',
      'Shoot the Moon: Taking all 26 penalty points gives 0 to shooter, 26 to everyone else.',
      'Passing direction rotates: Left → Right → Across → None (hold), then repeats.',
      '2 of Clubs always leads the first trick of each round.',
    ],
