    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Have the lowest cumulative score when any player reaches 100 points. Avoid taking tricks containing hearts (1 point each) and the Queen of Spades (13 points).',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. PASSING: After the deal, each player selects 3 cards to pass to an opponent (direction rotates: Left, Right, Across, None). All passes are simultaneous.\n2. OPENING LEAD: The player with the 2 of Clubs leads it to the first trick.\n3. FOLLOWING SUIT: Players must follow the suit led if possible. If unable to follow suit, any card may be played (except penalty cards on the first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick. There is no trump suit. The trick winner leads the next trick.\n5. BREAKING HEARTS: Hearts cannot be led until a heart has been played ('discarded') on a previous trick, or the player has nothing but hearts remaining.\n6. FIRST TRICK RESTRICTION: No penalty cards (hearts or Queen of Spades) may be played on the first trick.\n7. SCORING: After all 13 tricks are played, each player counts penalty points in their captured tricks. Each heart = 1 point, Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points.\n8. SHOOT THE MOON: If one player captures ALL 13 hearts AND the Queen of Spades, they score 0 and every other player scores 26 points.\n9. GAME END: Play continues across rounds until a player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest score at that point wins.",
      'Scoring example: Penalty-based scoring. Each heart captured = 1 point. Queen of Spades = 13 points. Maximum penalty per round = 26 points. Shoot the Moon reversal: if one player takes all 26, they get 0 and others get 26. Game ends when any player reaches 100 cumulative points. The player with the lowest cumulative score at that point wins..',
